kunzite: Adreno 710, after G4 (main repo ios/gpu-glue-plan.md): a GPU-UI boot without the wait for
the log, and the boot logo as a gauge. The window server is to start only once the GPU is kept
(userland/gpu/bbd_wrap.c waits for RedwoodGPU), so the time the kept run takes is time the boot
logo stays on. Keep mode now starts the run as soon as the root filesystem is mounted (the
firmware comes from it; kgpu_delay is then the most it waits, polled every 250 ms) instead of
kgpu_delay (60 s) after boot, and its pause before each group of reads is 0 unless kgpu_pause is
given: the steps are proven (boots #45-#53), and the pauses (1.5 s each) were most of the rest of
the 3 minutes RedwoodGPU took on #53. The logo gauge (kg_logo_*): at the start of a kept run the
logo is found in the panel memory (0xb8000000, write-combined: the box of the pixels that are not
black between x 140-940, y 400-2000) and kept; after each step the logo is drawn again, its
bottom done/last part amber (a pixel's brightness times the colour); once RedwoodGPU is published
it is all green, and red if the run ends short or keeps without RedwoodGPU. Nothing is drawn after
the window server's first frame: SweetFramebuffer's AppleCLCD::present sets sweet_fb_presented,
and the gauge then lets the panel go. Non-kept runs are unchanged.

